<!--
    MDT'S "SELECT ONE OR MORE APPLICATIONS TO INSTALL" PANE. DESIGN 11.2 lists
    this page and HDT had never drawn it; an admin arriving from MDT expects a
    checked list here and nothing else.

    THE LIST IS THE SHARE'S CATALOG. Get-HDTWizardApplication reads
    Applications\<Id>\app.yaml and hands the rows over as a field, the way
    Get-HDTWizardSequence fills the task sequence picker. This markup carries no
    rows at all - it used to carry three, typed by hand, and said so here: a
    share holding eleven applications offered three, two of which did not exist.

    AN ItemsControl, NOT A ListBox, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF THE SCREEN. A
    ListBox would give every row a selection highlight on top of its checkbox,
    so a row could be blue and unticked at the same time - two states meaning
    two different things, one of which does nothing. What this page collects is
    the TICKS. Nothing here has a "selected" row, so nothing here draws one.

    THE TICK LIVES ON THE ROW, NOT IN THE VISUAL TREE. IsChecked is bound TwoWay
    to the row's IsSelected, so what the technician ticks is on the object the
    host handed this control - which is what lets the answer be read back
    without walking anything, and tested without a screen.

    Content BINDS TO Text, WHICH IS THE NAME AND THE VERSION. The technician
    reads "7-Zip 24.09"; the sequence needs 7Zip-24.09, and that is Id on the
    same row, never parsed back out of a label somebody may translate.

    DynamicResource THROUGHOUT, BECAUSE A SHARE PAGE IS PARSED DETACHED.
    New-HDTWizardHost loads this file and only then puts it inside the shell, so
    at parse time there is no dictionary above it and a StaticResource throws
    where a page should be.
-->
<Grid xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
      xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
        <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
        <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

    <!--
        NO HINT ABOVE THE LIST, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. wizard.yaml's subheading
        already says "Everything published on the share. Nothing ticked is a
        normal answer" two lines higher, and a page that said it twice would be
        a screen explaining itself at the cost of the controls on it - which
        this repository has written down twice and which a photograph of the
        page made obvious. The one hint that survives is BELOW the list, because
        it says something the subheading does not: a rule's picks install
        whether or not they are ticked here.
    -->

    <!--
        THE BORDER IS THE FIELD, and it uses the theme's brushes rather than
        naming colours, so a page added later cannot drift a shade off the
        boxes beside it.
    -->
    <Border Grid.Row="1" Background="{DynamicResource HDTFooterBrush}"
            BorderBrush="{DynamicResource HDTBorderBrush}" BorderThickness="1">
        <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" Padding="10,8,10,8">
            <ItemsControl x:Name="HDTApplicationList">
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate>
                        <CheckBox Margin="0,5"
                                  IsChecked="{Binding IsSelected, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                  Content="{Binding Text}" />
                    </DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>
        </ScrollViewer>
    </Border>

    <!--
        WHAT AN EMPTY LIST MEANS, SAID ON THE SCREEN. Ticking nothing is a
        legitimate answer - a base image with no applications is most of what a
        lab deploys - and a technician who cannot tell "none selected" from
        "this page is broken" will go looking for the broken thing.
    -->
    <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Style="{DynamicResource HDTHintText}" Margin="0,10,0,0"
               TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="620" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
               Text="Applications a rule already selected are installed whether or not they are ticked here." />
</Grid>
